Public variable seedha hota hai, koi extra logic nahi hota. @property se aap validation ya calculation add kar sakte ho, aur future mein implementation badalna easy hota hai. Lekin agar aapko simple storage chahiye, to direct variable thoda fast aur simple hota hai.
```python
class Person:
    def __init__(self, name):
        self._name = name
    @property
    def name(self):
        return self._name
    @name.setter
    def name(self, value):
        if value:
            self._name = value
```

Equality check __eq__ se hoti hai. Example:
```python
class Point:
    def __init__(self, x, y):
        self.x, self.y = x, y
    def __eq__(self, other):
        return self.x == other.x and self.y == other.y
```
Ab Point(1,2) == Point(1,2) True return karega.
